  "text": "Lydia heard one sermon by a river and bankrolled the mission. Acts sixteen. Paul and his companions arrive in Philippi, and on the sabbath they go out of the city by a river side, where prayer was customarily made. They sit down and speak to the women who gathered there. And a certain woman named Lydia heard them. She is a seller of purple from the city of Thyatira, which is the luxury goods trade of the ancient world, and she worshipped God. And the text says the Lord opened her heart, that she attended unto the things which were spoken of Paul. She is baptized, and her household with her. And then she makes an offer that is really not an offer. If ye have judged me to be faithful to the Lord, come into my house, and abide there. And the text adds four words. And she constrained us. She talked them into it. Later in the chapter, after Paul and Silas get out of prison, where do they go? They entered into the house of Lydia. Her house was the base. Not asked. Told.",
